Did you give the box with the bird in it to the robot?

Did you train the robot to copy the zero and set it down?

Did you train the robot to copy the sensor and drop the copy
on the zero on the floor?

Did you pick up the number from the floor and give it to the bird?

Did you remember to press 'Escape' to finish training the robot?

Did you give the box back to the robot and wait for the bird to
put at least 5 numbers on her nest?  By the way did
you see that the sensor in the thought bubble became blank all by itself?

Well what I would do is this.  I'd give the box with the bird to the
robot.  Then I'd train the robot to copy the zero and set the copy
down on the floor.  Then I'd copy the sensor and drop it on the zero.
Then I'd pick up the result and give it to the bird.  Then I'd press
'Escape' since I'd be done training the robot.  I'd give the robot the
box and wait for Dusty to appear.  Then I'd vacuum out the zero and
give the box back to the robot.  After the bird has put at least 5
numbers on her nest I'd pick up the box with the nest.

